Here's a sample script in HTML that can be used to deny access to a website or service:

```
<!-- Deny Access Script -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Access Denied</title>
	<style>
		body {
			background-color: #f0f0f0;
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
		}
		.container {
			width: 80%;
			margin: 40px auto;
			text-align: center;
		}
		h1 {
			color: #e74c3c;
		}
		p {
			margin-bottom: 20px;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="container">
		<h1>Access Denied</h1>
		<p>You do not have permission to access this website or service. Please contact the administrator for further assistance.</p>
		<p>Reason: [Insert reason here, e.g. invalid username/password, unauthorized IP address, etc.]</p>
	</div>
</body>
</html>
```

This script can be used as an HTML page to deny access to a website or service. The script uses CSS styles and HTML elements to display a message indicating that access has been denied.

Note: This script should be placed in the root directory of your website, and should be renamed to `index.html` to ensure that it is served as the default page when accessed without specifying a specific file.
